Package: labtracker
Type: Package
Title: Fail-Soft Lab Tracker Figure Capture for R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Samuel", "Brudner", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "samuel.brudner@gmail.com")
Description: Captures figures saved with ggplot2::ggsave() and the png(),
    jpeg(), tiff(), bmp() and pdf() file devices into Lab Tracker as staged
    evidence notes by running the Python client's 'lt capture file' command
    in the background. Captures only saves whose project is bound (an
    explicit project, LAB_TRACKER_PROJECT_ID, or the checkout's lt_ids.json)
    and never raises an error into the R session.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: grDevices
Suggests: ggplot2, testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
